# Módulos de Detección — Estándares

## Interfaz mínima requerida (todo detector)

```python
class MiDetector:
    def find_pose(self, img: np.ndarray, draw: bool = True) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, Any]:
        """Procesa frame. Retorna (frame_procesado, results)."""
        ...

    def find_position(self, img: np.ndarray, results: Any, draw: bool = True
                      ) -> Tuple[List, Dict[str, Any]]:
        """Retorna (lm_list, bbox). bbox debe incluir 'is_falling' si aplica."""
        ...

    def close(self) -> None: ...
    def __enter__(self): return self
    def __exit__(self, *_): self.close()
```

## Formato de bbox estándar
```python
bbox = {
    "xmin": int, "ymin": int, "xmax": int, "ymax": int,
    "width": int, "height": int,
    "is_falling": bool,          # solo detectores de caída
    "track_id": int,             # si hay tracking
}
```

## Validación temporal (patrón obligatorio para reducir falsos +)
```python
from collections import deque
window = deque(maxlen=self.min_fall_frames)
window.append(is_falling_this_frame)
confirmed = len(window) == self.min_fall_frames and all(window)
```

